IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2: ss 379 to 386 -- the register of members of a foreign company, the index, the evidence the register and a certificate give,
-- bearer shares, the regulations that may apply other provisions of the Act, and the general penalty. Part sgg, layer 1.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the section's own test met; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (tagged FALSE-kind);
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say" (tagged NOTHING-kind). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Section 379: the register of members`

DECLARE `s 379 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 379(1)(a) keep a register of its members at its registered office in Singapore or at some other place in Singapore`
    `s 379(1)(b) lodge a notice with the Registrar specifying the address at which the register of members is kept`
    `s 379(3) lodge a notice of the change in the address at which the register of members is kept`

-- (1) "A foreign company registered under this Division on or after 31 March 2017 must, within 30 days after it is registered —"; (2) "before 31 March 2017 must, within 60 days after that date —".
-- src:25191 | Register of members of foreign companies
-- src:25193 | 379.—(1) A foreign company registered under this Division on or
-- src:25194 | after 31 March 2017 must, within 30 days after it is registered —
-- src:25196 | (a) keep a register of its members at its registered office in
-- src:25197 | Singapore or at some other place in Singapore; and
-- src:25199 | (b) lodge a notice with the Registrar specifying the address at
-- src:25200 | which the register of members is kept.
@ref s 379(1) (src:25191-25200)
GIVEN `the day the foreign company was registered under this Division` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(1) the foreign company must keep a register of its members and lodge the notice within 30 days after it is registered` MEANS
    IF `the day the foreign company was registered under this Division` AT LEAST (Date 31 3 2017)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A foreign company registered under this Division on or after 31 March 2017 must, within 30 days after it is registered —" (a duty gated by the date it names: fork F-D1)

@ref s 379(1)(a) (src:25196-25197)
GIVEN `the register is kept at its registered office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is kept at some other place in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(1)(a) the register of members is kept at a place the paragraph allows` MEANS
    IF `the register is kept at its registered office in Singapore` OR `the register is kept at some other place in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) keep a register of its members at its registered office in Singapore or at some other place in Singapore" (a duty not met: a register kept outside Singapore is neither place)

@ref s 379(1) (src:25193-25200)
GIVEN `the day the foreign company was registered under this Division` IS A DATE
      `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(1) the act was done within 30 days after the foreign company was registered` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the foreign company was registered under this Division` `the day the act was done` 30 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 30 days after it is registered" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); "within 30 days after" is counted as "not later than 30 days after": fork F-P1)

@ref s 379(1)(a) (src:25196-25197)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 379 act`
`s 379(1)(a) the foreign company must keep a register of its members within 30 days after it is registered` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 379(1)(a) keep a register of its members at its registered office in Singapore or at some other place in Singapore`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the register of members was not kept within 30 days after the foreign company was registered"

@ref s 379(1)(b) (src:25199-25200)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 379 act`
`s 379(1)(b) the foreign company must lodge a notice of the address of the register within 30 days after it is registered` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 379(1)(b) lodge a notice with the Registrar specifying the address at which the register of members is kept`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the notice of the address of the register of members was not lodged within 30 days after the foreign company was registered"

-- src:25207 | (2) A foreign company registered under this Division before
-- src:25208 | 31 March 2017 must, within 60 days after that date —
-- src:25210 | (a) keep a register of its members at its registered office in
-- src:25211 | Singapore or at some other place in Singapore; and
-- src:25213 | (b) lodge a notice with the Registrar specifying the address at
-- src:25214 | which the register of members is kept.
@ref s 379(2) (src:25207-25214)
GIVEN `the day the foreign company was registered under this Division` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(2) the foreign company must keep a register of its members and lodge the notice within 60 days after 31 March 2017` MEANS
    IF `the day the foreign company was registered under this Division` LESS THAN (Date 31 3 2017)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A foreign company registered under this Division before 31 March 2017 must, within 60 days after that date —" (a duty gated by the date it names: fork F-D1)

@ref s 379(2) (src:25207-25208)
GIVEN `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(2) the act was done within 60 days after 31 March 2017` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (Date 31 3 2017) `the day the act was done` 60 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 60 days after that date" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P1)

-- The two duties of (2) are the same acts as those of (1); the trace starts on 31 March 2017, and the 60 days run from that day.
@ref s 379(2)(a) (src:25210-25211)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 379 act`
`s 379(2)(a) the foreign company must keep a register of its members within 60 days after 31 March 2017` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 379(1)(a) keep a register of its members at its registered office in Singapore or at some other place in Singapore`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the register of members was not kept within 60 days after 31 March 2017"

@ref s 379(2)(b) (src:25213-25214)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 379 act`
`s 379(2)(b) the foreign company must lodge a notice of the address of the register within 60 days after 31 March 2017` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 379(1)(b) lodge a notice with the Registrar specifying the address at which the register of members is kept`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the notice of the address of the register of members was not lodged within 60 days after 31 March 2017"

-- src:25218 | (3) If there is any change in the address at which the register of
-- src:25219 | members mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) is kept, the foreign
-- src:25220 | company must, within 30 days after the change, lodge a notice of the
-- src:25221 | change with the Registrar.
@ref s 379(3) (src:25218-25221)
GIVEN `there is a change in the address at which the register of members mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) is kept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(3) the foreign company must lodge a notice of the change with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `there is a change in the address at which the register of members mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) is kept`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is any change in the address at which the register of members ... is kept, the foreign company must, within 30 days after the change, lodge a notice of the change with the Registrar" (a duty gated by "If": fork F-D1)

@ref s 379(3) (src:25218-25221)
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of the change was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(3) the notice of the change was lodged within 30 days after the change` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the change` `the day the notice of the change was lodged` 30 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 30 days after the change, lodge a notice of the change with the Registrar" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P1)

@ref s 379(3) (src:25218-25221)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 379 act`
`s 379(3) the foreign company must lodge a notice of the change of address within 30 days after the change` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 379(3) lodge a notice of the change in the address at which the register of members is kept`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the notice of the change in the address of the register of members was not lodged within 30 days after the change"

§ `Section 380: contents of the register and the index of members`

DECLARE `s 380 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 380(2)(a) keep an index in convenient form of the names of the members`
    `s 380(2)(b) make the necessary alteration in the index`
    `s 380(2)(c) keep the index at the same place as the register of members`
    `s 380(4) update the register of members to reflect the change`

-- (1) the register "must contain the following particulars": (a) names and addresses; (b) the date each person's name was entered; (c) the date on which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased;
-- (d) in the case of a foreign company having a share capital, (i) a statement of the shares held and the amount paid, and (ii) such particulars of the shares, including the date of every allotment; (e) such other particulars as may be prescribed.
-- src:25225 | Contents of register and index of members of foreign
-- src:25226 | companies
-- src:25228 | 380.—(1) The register of members of a foreign company required
-- src:25229 | to be kept under section 379 must contain the following particulars:
-- src:25231 | (a) the names and addresses of the members of the foreign
-- src:25232 | company;
-- src:25234 | (b) the date on which the name of each person was entered in
-- src:25235 | the register as a member;
-- src:25237 | (c) the date on which any person who ceased to be a member
-- src:25238 | during the previous 7 years so ceased to be a member;
-- src:25240 | (d) in the case of a foreign company having a share capital —
-- src:25242 | (i) a statement of the shares held by each member,
-- src:25243 | distinguishing each share by its number (if any) or by
-- src:25244 | the number (if any) of the certificate evidencing the
-- src:25245 | member’s holding and of the amount paid or agreed
-- src:25246 | to be considered as paid on the shares of each
-- src:25247 | member; and
-- src:25249 | (ii) such particulars of the shares held by each member,
-- src:25250 | including the date of every allotment of shares to
-- src:25251 | members and the number of shares comprised in
-- src:25252 | each allotment;
-- src:25257 | (e) such other particulars as may be prescribed.
@ref s 380(1) (src:25225-25257)
GIVEN `the register contains the names and addresses of the members of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains the date on which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains the date on which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share, and of the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains such particulars of the shares held by each member as paragraph (d)(ii) requires, including the date of every allotment and the number of shares in each` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register contains every other particular that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(1) the register of members contains the particulars the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the register contains the names and addresses of the members of the foreign company`
      AND `the register contains the date on which the name of each person was entered in the register as a member`
      AND `the register contains the date on which any person who ceased to be a member during the previous 7 years so ceased`
      AND ((NOT `the foreign company has a share capital`) OR (`the register contains a statement of the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share, and of the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid` AND `the register contains such particulars of the shares held by each member as paragraph (d)(ii) requires, including the date of every allotment and the number of shares in each`))
      AND `the register contains every other particular that may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The register of members of a foreign company required to be kept under section 379 must contain the following particulars:" (a requirement not met; paragraph (d) reaches only a company having a share capital; the particulars prescribed under paragraph (e) are not in the sources)

-- (2) "Every foreign company having more than 50 members must, unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index — (a) keep an index ...; (b) within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members, make any necessary alteration in the index; and (c) keep the index at the same place as the register of members."
-- src:25261 | (2) Every foreign company having more than 50 members must,
-- src:25262 | unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in
-- src:25263 | itself an index —
-- src:25265 | (a) keep an index in convenient form of the names of the
-- src:25266 | members;
-- src:25268 | (b) within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is
-- src:25269 | made in the register of members, make any necessary
-- src:25270 | alteration in the index; and
-- src:25272 | (c) keep the index at the same place as the register of
-- src:25273 | members.
@ref s 380(2) (src:25261-25273)
GIVEN `the number of members of the foreign company` IS A NUMBER
      `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(2) the foreign company must keep an index of the names of its members` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the foreign company` GREATER THAN 50 AND (NOT `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every foreign company having more than 50 members must, unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index —" (a duty gated by "having more than 50 members" and an "unless": fork F-D1)

@ref s 380(2)(b) (src:25268-25270)
GIVEN `the day the alteration was made in the register of members` IS A DATE
      `the day the necessary alteration was made in the index` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(2)(b) the index was altered within 14 days after the alteration of the register` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the alteration was made in the register of members` `the day the necessary alteration was made in the index` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members, make any necessary alteration in the index" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P1)

@ref s 380(2)(a) (src:25265-25266)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 380 act`
`s 380(2)(a) the foreign company must keep an index in convenient form of the names of its members` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 380(2)(a) keep an index in convenient form of the names of the members`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 380(2)(a) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 380(2)(b) (src:25268-25270)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 380 act`
`s 380(2)(b) the foreign company must make the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days after the alteration of the register` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 380(2)(b) make the necessary alteration in the index`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the necessary alteration was not made in the index within 14 days after the alteration of the register"

@ref s 380(2)(c) (src:25272-25273)
GIVEN `the index is kept at the same place as the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(2)(c) the index is kept where paragraph (c) requires` MEANS
    IF `the index is kept at the same place as the register of members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) keep the index at the same place as the register of members" (a duty not met)

@ref s 380(2)(c) (src:25272-25273)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 380 act`
`s 380(2)(c) the foreign company must keep the index at the same place as the register of members` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 380(2)(c) keep the index at the same place as the register of members`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 380(2)(c) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:25277 | (3) The index must in respect of each member contain a sufficient
-- src:25278 | indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be
-- src:25279 | readily found.
@ref s 380(3) (src:25277-25279)
GIVEN `the index contains, in respect of each member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(3) the index contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the index contains, in respect of each member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The index must in respect of each member contain a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found" (a requirement not met)

-- src:25283 | (4) If there is any change in the particulars mentioned in
-- src:25284 | subsection (1) contained in the register of members of a foreign
-- src:25285 | company, the foreign company must, within 30 days after the change,
-- src:25286 | update the register of members to reflect the change.
@ref s 380(4) (src:25283-25286)
GIVEN `there is a change in the particulars mentioned in subsection (1) contained in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(4) the foreign company must update the register of members to reflect the change` MEANS
    IF `there is a change in the particulars mentioned in subsection (1) contained in the register of members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is any change in the particulars mentioned in subsection (1) contained in the register of members of a foreign company, the foreign company must, within 30 days after the change, update the register" (a duty gated by "If": fork F-D1)

@ref s 380(4) (src:25283-25286)
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the day the register was updated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(4) the register was updated within 30 days after the change` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the change` `the day the register was updated` 30 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 30 days after the change, update the register of members to reflect the change" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P1)

@ref s 380(4) (src:25283-25286)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 380 act`
`s 380(4) the foreign company must update the register of members within 30 days after the change` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 380(4) update the register of members to reflect the change`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the register of members was not updated within 30 days after the change"

§ `Sections 381 and 382: the register and a certificate as evidence`

-- src:25290 | Register to be prima facie evidence
-- src:25292 | 381. A register of members of a foreign company kept under
-- src:25293 | section 379 is prima facie evidence of any matter which the register is
-- src:25294 | required under this Division to be contained.
@ref s 381 (src:25290-25294)
GIVEN `the register of members was kept under section 379` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one which the register is required under this Division to contain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 381 the register is prima facie evidence of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the register of members was kept under section 379` AND `the matter is one which the register is required under this Division to contain`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A register of members of a foreign company kept under section 379 is prima facie evidence of any matter which the register is required under this Division to be contained" says nothing of another register or another matter

-- 382 "A certificate made under the seal of a foreign company (or in any manner permitted for certificates of such type by the laws of the country or territory in which the foreign company is incorporated or established) specifying any shares held by any member of that company and registered in the register of members ... kept under section 379 is prima facie evidence of the title of the member to the shares and the registration of the shares in that register."
-- src:25298 | Certificate as to shareholding
-- src:25300 | 382. A certificate made under the seal of a foreign company (or in
-- src:25301 | any manner permitted for certificates of such type by the laws of the
-- src:25302 | country or territory in which the foreign company is incorporated or
-- src:25303 | established) specifying any shares held by any member of that
-- src:25304 | company and registered in the register of members of the foreign
-- src:25305 | company kept under section 379 is prima facie evidence of the title of
-- src:25310 | the member to the shares and the registration of the shares in that
-- src:25311 | register.
@ref s 382 (src:25298-25311)
GIVEN `the certificate is made under the seal of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is made in a manner permitted for certificates of such type by the laws of the country or territory in which the foreign company is incorporated or established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate specifies shares held by a member of the company and registered in the register of members kept under section 379` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382 the certificate is prima facie evidence of the title of the member to the shares and the registration of the shares in the register` MEANS
    IF (`the certificate is made under the seal of the foreign company` OR `the certificate is made in a manner permitted for certificates of such type by the laws of the country or territory in which the foreign company is incorporated or established`) AND `the certificate specifies shares held by a member of the company and registered in the register of members kept under section 379`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate made under the seal of a foreign company (or in any manner permitted ...) specifying any shares held by any member ... and registered in the register of members ... kept under section 379 is prima facie evidence" says nothing of another certificate

§ `Section 383: bearer shares and share warrants`

-- src:25315 | No civil proceedings to be brought in respect of bearer shares
-- src:25316 | or share warrants
-- src:25318 | 383.—(1) Any allotment, issue, sale, transfer, assignment or other
-- src:25319 | disposition in Singapore of any bearer share or share warrant by a
-- src:25320 | foreign company registered under this Division is void.
@ref s 383(1) (src:25315-25320)
GIVEN `the disposition is an allotment, issue, sale, transfer, assignment or other disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disposition is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing disposed of is a bearer share or share warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disposition is by a foreign company registered under this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 383(1) the disposition is void` MEANS
    IF `the disposition is an allotment, issue, sale, transfer, assignment or other disposition` AND `the disposition is in Singapore` AND `the thing disposed of is a bearer share or share warrant` AND `the disposition is by a foreign company registered under this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any allotment, issue, sale, transfer, assignment or other disposition in Singapore of any bearer share or share warrant by a foreign company registered under this Division is void" says nothing of a disposition outside Singapore, of another security or by another company

-- (2) "No civil proceedings may be brought or maintained in any court for or in respect of any bearer share or share warrant allotted, issued, sold, transferred, assigned or disposed by a foreign company registered under this Division." A bar, answered in the bar's direction.
-- src:25324 | (2) No civil proceedings may be brought or maintained in any court
-- src:25325 | for or in respect of any bearer share or share warrant allotted, issued,
-- src:25326 | sold, transferred, assigned or disposed by a foreign company
-- src:25327 | registered under this Division.
@ref s 383(2) (src:25324-25327)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil proceedings in a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are for or in respect of a bearer share or share warrant allotted, issued, sold, transferred, assigned or disposed by a foreign company registered under this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 383(2) the civil proceedings may not be brought or maintained` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are civil proceedings in a court` AND `the proceedings are for or in respect of a bearer share or share warrant allotted, issued, sold, transferred, assigned or disposed by a foreign company registered under this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "No civil proceedings may be brought or maintained in any court for or in respect of any bearer share or share warrant" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar names civil proceedings in a court in respect of such shares or warrants of a foreign company registered under this Division, without "only"

§ `Sections 384 and 385: regulations that may apply other provisions or exempt`

-- 384 "Regulations made under section 411 may — (a) provide for — (i) the application of any provision of Division 7 of Part 4 relating to the transfer of shares in a company to the transfer of shares in a foreign company;
-- and (ii) the application of Division 4 of Part 5 relating to the register of members to the register of members of a foreign company, subject to such adaptations, modifications or additions as may be prescribed; and (b) exempt any foreign company or class of foreign companies from all or any provision of this Division."
-- Whether regulations have been made is a supplied fact: the regulations are not among the sources.
-- src:25331 | Application of provisions of Act
-- src:25333 | 384. Regulations made under section 411 may —
-- src:25335 | (a) provide for —
-- src:25337 | (i) the application of any provision of Division 7 of
-- src:25338 | Part 4 relating to the transfer of shares in a company
-- src:25339 | to the transfer of shares in a foreign company; and
-- src:25341 | (ii) the application of Division 4 of Part 5 relating to the
-- src:25342 | register of members to the register of members of a
-- src:25343 | foreign company,
-- src:25345 | (a) subject to such adaptations, modifications or additions as
-- src:25346 | may be prescribed; and
-- src:25348 | (b) exempt any foreign company or class of foreign companies
-- src:25349 | from all or any provision of this Division.
@ref s 384 (src:25331-25349)
GIVEN `regulations made under section 411 provide for the application of the provision of Division 7 of Part 4 to the transfer of shares in the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(a)(i) the provision of Division 7 of Part 4 relating to the transfer of shares applies to the transfer of shares in the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `regulations made under section 411 provide for the application of the provision of Division 7 of Part 4 to the transfer of shares in the foreign company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations made under section 411 are not among the sources, and the text does not say there are any

@ref s 384 (src:25331-25349)
GIVEN `regulations made under section 411 provide for the application of the provision of Division 4 of Part 5 to the register of members of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(a)(ii) the provision of Division 4 of Part 5 relating to the register of members applies to the register of members of the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `regulations made under section 411 provide for the application of the provision of Division 4 of Part 5 to the register of members of the foreign company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations made under section 411 are not among the sources, and the text does not say there are any

@ref s 384 (src:25331-25349)
GIVEN `regulations made under section 411 exempt the foreign company, or a class of foreign companies to which it belongs, from the provision of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(b) the foreign company is exempt from the provision of this Division` MEANS
    IF `regulations made under section 411 exempt the foreign company, or a class of foreign companies to which it belongs, from the provision of this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations made under section 411 are not among the sources, and the text does not say there are any

§ `Section 386: penalties`

DECLARE `s 386 provision of this Division` IS ONE OF
    `s 368A(5) a director's or authorised representative's failure to give the information`
    `s 372(1C) a director's or authorised representative's default in complying with subsection (1A)`
    `s 373(18) a default in complying with section 373, other than subsection (7A)`
    `s 373(18A) a default in complying with section 373(7A)`
    `s 378(7) a failure to comply with section 378(4)`
    `s 386 some other provision of this Division`

DECLARE `s 386 penalty` HAS
    `s 386 the offence applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 386 the maximum fine, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 386 the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 386 a default penalty also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- "other than a provision in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned": the provisions of this Division that mention one are ss 368A(5), 372(1C), 373(18), 373(18A) and 378(7) (lines 23890, 24164, 24472, 24487 and 25082 of the text).
-- src:25355 | Penalties
-- src:25357 | 386. If default is made by any foreign company in complying with
-- src:25358 | any provision of this Division, other than a provision in which a
-- src:25359 | penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned, the company and
-- src:25364 | every officer of the company who is in default and every authorised
-- src:25365 | representative of the company who knowingly and wilfully
-- src:25366 | authorises or permits the default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:25367 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to
-- src:25368 | a default penalty.
@ref s 386 (src:25355-25368)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 386 provision of this Division`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386 a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned in the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 368A(5) a director's or authorised representative's failure to give the information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 372(1C) a director's or authorised representative's default in complying with subsection (1A)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 373(18) a default in complying with section 373, other than subsection (7A)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 373(18A) a default in complying with section 373(7A)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 378(7) a failure to comply with section 378(4)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 386 some other provision of this Division` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the provision mentions no penalty or punishment, so the section's carve-out does not apply to it

@ref s 386 (src:25355-25368)
GIVEN `the elements of the offence are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 386 penalty`
`s 386 the penalty if the element is met` MEANS
    IF `the elements of the offence are met`
    THEN `s 386 penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 1000, NOTHING, JUST TRUE   -- "shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty"; no term of imprisonment is stated (NOTHING-kind (silent)); the default penalty's amount is not in the text
    ELSE `s 386 penalty` OF JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made by any foreign company in complying with any provision of this Division, other than a provision in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned, the company and every officer of the company who is in default and every authorised representative of the company who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of an offence: split site (i), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S1)

@ref s 386 (src:25355-25368)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `default is made by the foreign company in complying with a provision of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 386 penalty`
`s 386 the offence and its penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role of the person`
    WHEN `s 365 role: the foreign company` THEN `s 386 the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with a provision of this Division` AND (NOT `the provision is one in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned`))
    WHEN `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company` THEN `s 386 the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with a provision of this Division` AND (NOT `the provision is one in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned`) AND `the officer is in default`)
    WHEN `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` THEN `s 386 the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with a provision of this Division` AND (NOT `the provision is one in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned`) AND `the officer is in default`)   -- s 4(1) "officer" includes "a director of the corporation": a director is an officer of the company (fork F-O1)
    WHEN `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` THEN `s 386 the penalty if the element is met` (`default is made by the foreign company in complying with a provision of this Division` AND (NOT `the provision is one in which a penalty or punishment is expressly mentioned`) AND `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default`)
    OTHERWISE `s 386 penalty` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company and every officer of the company who is in default and every authorised representative of the company who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default" names the persons it reaches, without "only"
